{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on AE-1 question `d6103136`: neither yet. The next bounded\nwork is an attribution audit under AE-1.\n\nI rule on no charge and on no cap without the numbers by charge site.\nRuling `50ce6650` stands: AE-1 classifies no budget refusal, and ARC-1\nowns the question of fit.\n\n1. AE-1's shared runtime and clone acceptance stays as written and\n   stays failing. Change no cap, deadline, assertion, credit or cache.\n   AE-1 does not gate while those five cases fail.\n2. The audit, for the Base prefix at seq 1 and the Grow prefix at\n   seq 0: each debit of `nodes` and of `inputWork` by charge site,\n   from the installed-policy proof through the plan to the finish\n   quote. The sum of the sites equals the totals of END `755cb512`.\n3. State whether one pass charges the same nodes or the same bytes at\n   two sites. Name the sites and the amounts.\n4. State the smallest `nodes` cap and the smallest `inputWork` cap at\n   which each prefix confirms. One diagnostic run with a larger\n   budget in the fixture is in order for that number. It is a\n   diagnosis and not an acceptance, and its change does not land.\n5. State how the two walks grow: what a longer creator chain or a\n   larger installed package adds to each site.\n\nRead-only work and the one diagnostic run. No production change.\n\nWith those numbers I assign the repair. A duplicate charge is an AE-1\nrepair. A fit that needs a larger cap is a cap decision for Hugh. A\nprefix that cannot fit one pass belongs to the ARC-1 predicate and\nits named stop.\n\nAE-1's proof-binding and metadata controls proceed at the passing\nowner. P1's own delta does not wait for this.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}